capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/state.json" "file_sha256" "b171229f63f2bc948afae3f1e5f84b115b2783e80bc4c5ea285748cf8ab15c71" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/state.json" "file_sha256" "b171229f63f2bc948afae3f1e5f84b115b2783e80bc4c5ea285748cf8ab15c71" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/state.json" "file_sha256" "b171229f63f2bc948afae3f1e5f84b115b2783e80bc4c5ea285748cf8ab15c71" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x)=x-{e}^{x},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=0$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(0)<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/state.json" "file_sha256" "b171229f63f2bc948afae3f1e5f84b115b2783e80bc4c5ea285748cf8ab15c71" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to identify whether $x=0$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=x-{e}^{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=1-{e}^{x},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-{e}^{x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x} & =1 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have a critical point at $x=0.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=-{e}^{x},\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=0$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(0)=-1<0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is negative at $x=0,$ so this critical point is a relative *maximum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=0$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(0)<0\\,✓$\n\n- $f(0)$ has a relative *maximum* at $x=0\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/state.json" "file_sha256" "b171229f63f2bc948afae3f1e5f84b115b2783e80bc4c5ea285748cf8ab15c71" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "62bff426ce2a3d3733958909ae26160db95e94c280c7f7746696465f5547d25c" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114414" "field" "selection"