emy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/state.json" "file_sha256" "b171229f63f2bc948afae3f1e5f84b115b2783e80bc4c5ea285748cf8ab15c71" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-22079" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/state.json" "file_sha256" "b171229f63f2bc948afae3f1e5f84b115b2783e80bc4c5ea285748cf8ab15c71" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-22079" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/state.json" "file_sha256" "b171229f63f2bc948afae3f1e5f84b115b2783e80bc4c5ea285748cf8ab15c71" "basis" 1229 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-22011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x)=12{x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=-6$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(-6)<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=-6$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063420/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9597b17763f313c905f4458d5fc007a70ed64f4e9fadd789bee6ac5a4832ac7" "basis" 2048 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063420/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-22011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to identify whether $x=-6$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=12{x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=36{x}^{2}-{x}^{4},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}36{x}^{2}-{x}^{4} & =0 \\\\ -{x}^{2}({x}^{2}-36) & =0 \\\\ -{x}^{2}(x+6)(x-6) & =0 \\\\ x & =-6,0,6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=-6,0,6.$ We're interested in the critical point $x=-6.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=72x-4{x}^{3},\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=-6$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(-6)=432>0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is positive at $x=-6,$ so this critical point is a relative *minimum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=-6$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(-6)<0\\,\\times $\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative *minimum* at $x=-6\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063420/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9597b17763f313c905f4458d5fc007a70ed64f4e9fadd789bee6ac5a4832ac7" "basis" 2048 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063420/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-22011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063420/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6131c752b2ad11b6dd9ae76a11fa6575707e40fd57802095aeadd10ef7b685de" "basis" 2048 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063420/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-22011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063420/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9597b17763f313c905f4458d5fc007a70ed64f4e9fadd789bee6ac5a4832ac7" "basis" 2048 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063420/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-22011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063420/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9597b17763f313c905f4458d5fc007a70ed64f4e9fadd789bee6ac5a4832ac7" "basis" 2048 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063420/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-22011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063420/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9597b17763f313c905f4458d5fc007a70ed64f4e9fadd789bee6ac5a4832ac7" "basis" 2048 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063420/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-22011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063420/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9597b17763f313c905f4458d5fc007a70ed64f4e9fadd789bee6ac5a4832ac7" "basis" 2048 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063420/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-22011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063420/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9597b17763f313c905f4458d5fc007a70ed64f4e9fadd789bee6ac5a4832ac7" "basis" 2048 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063420/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-22011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "None of the statements are true"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063420/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9597b17763f313c905f4458d5fc007a70ed64f4e9fadd789bee6ac5a4832ac7" "basis" 2048 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063420/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-21536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+8.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(1)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(1)<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=1$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-21536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We're given that $x=1$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)={x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+8,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+2x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=12{x}^{2}-12x+2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1) & =12(1)^{2}-12(1)+2 \\\\  & =2>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is positive, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-21536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b684e92b8f6096aef827a5c1de4bf5e093ddea5c38b04d380c93c7b050726776"} {"question" "q-21536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-21536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-21536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-22011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x)=12{x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=-6$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(-6)<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=-6$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-22011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to identify whether $x=-6$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=12{x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=36{x}^{2}-{x}^{4},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}36{x}^{2}-{x}^{4} & =0 \\\\ -{x}^{2}({x}^{2}-36) & =0 \\\\ -{x}^{2}(x+6)(x-6) & =0 \\\\ x & =-6,0,6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=-6,0,6.$ We're interested in the critical point $x=-6.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=72x-4{x}^{3},\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=-6$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(-6)=432>0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is positive at $x=-6,$ so this critical point is a relative *minimum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=-6$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(-6)<0\\,\\times $\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative *minimum* at $x=-6\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-22011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b684e92b8f6096aef827a5c1de4bf5e093ddea5c38b04d380c93c7b050726776"} {"question" "q-22011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-22011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "None of the statements are true"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-22011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-22079" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x)={x}^{3},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=0$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(0)<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-22079" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to identify whether $x=0$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)={x}^{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=3{x}^{2},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have a critical point at $x=0.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=6x,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=0$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(0)=0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is zero, so we should apply the first derivative test.\n\nLet's evaluate the first derivative at auxiliary points $\\pm 1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & =3(-1)^{2}=3>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(1) & =3(1)^{2}=3>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the first derivative does not change the sign at $x=0,$ $f(x)$ has no relative extrema.\n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=0$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(0)=0\\,\\times $\n\n- $f(x)$ has no relative extrema at $x=0\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-22079" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b684e92b8f6096aef827a5c1de4bf5e093ddea5c38b04d380c93c7b050726776"} {"question" "q-22079" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-22079" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-22079" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-22084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function $f(x)=3{x}^{4/3}-24{x}^{1/3}-6{x}^{-2/3}$ defined on $(0,\\infty ).$ Given that ${f}^{′}(1)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(1)=0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=1$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-22084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We're given that $x=1$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=3{x}^{4/3}-24{x}^{1/3}-6{x}^{-2/3},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=4{x}^{1/3}-8{x}^{-2/3}+4{x}^{-5/3}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{-2/3}+\\frac{16}{3}{x}^{-5/3}-\\frac{20}{3}{x}^{-8/3}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1) & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot (1)^{-2/3}+\\frac{16}{3}\\cdot (1)^{-5/3}-\\frac{20}{3}\\cdot (1)^{-8/3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is zero, we conclude that the test is inconclusive, we need to use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's  find the stationary points. These points are the solution of the equation ${f}^{′}(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{1/3}-8{x}^{-2/3}+4{x}^{-5/3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{-5/3}(4{x}^{2}-8x+4) & =0 \\\\ 4{x}^{-5/3}{(x-1)}^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the only stationary point on $(0,\\infty )$ is $x=1.$\n\nLet's choose auxiliary points from each side of the stationary point and evaluate the first derivative at them. We take the auxiliary points $x=\\frac{1}{2},2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}) & =4{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-5/3}{(\\frac{1}{2}-1)}^{2} \\\\  & =4{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-5/3}{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{{2}^{-5/3}})(\\frac{1}{{2}^{2}}) \\\\  & ={2}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{5/3}\\cdot {2}^{-2} \\\\  & ={2}^{5/3}>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =4\\cdot {2}^{-5/3}(2-1)^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2-5/3} \\\\  & ={2}^{1/3}>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the first derivative does not change the sign at $x=1$, we conclude that $f(x)$ has no relative extrema at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-22084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b684e92b8f6096aef827a5c1de4bf5e093ddea5c38b04d380c93c7b050726776"} {"question" "q-22084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-22084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-22084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-114414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x)=x-{e}^{x},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=0$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(0)<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-114414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to identify whether $x=0$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=x-{e}^{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=1-{e}^{x},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-{e}^{x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x} & =1 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have a critical point at $x=0.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=-{e}^{x},\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=0$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(0)=-1<0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is negative at $x=0,$ so this critical point is a relative *maximum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=0$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(0)<0\\,✓$\n\n- $f(0)$ has a relative *maximum* at $x=0\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-114414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b684e92b8f6096aef827a5c1de4bf5e093ddea5c38b04d380c93c7b050726776"} {"question" "q-114414" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-114414" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "None of the statements are true"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d19c358538dffd936a298061c1081ea24bb497fb17033c76d1a7061c29faa3"} {"question" "q-114414" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066801/state.json" "file_sha25